1
00:00:11,469 --> 00:00:12,303
[grunts]

2
00:00:13,054 --> 00:00:14,931
Hold all my calls.

3
00:00:15,014 --> 00:00:17,726
[giggling]

4
00:00:17,809 --> 00:00:19,394
♪ Boss Baby ♪

5
00:00:19,477 --> 00:00:23,523
♪ I'm the boss, Boss Baby
Boss boss, Boss Baby, boss boss ♪

6
00:00:23,606 --> 00:00:28,653
♪ Watch a itty-bitty kid get large
I'm the big Boss Baby in charge ♪

7
00:00:28,737 --> 00:00:31,072
♪ Stroller rolling
Up and down the boulevard ♪

8
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:33,742
♪ I'm the big Boss Baby in charge ♪

9
00:00:34,325 --> 00:00:39,581
♪ I run this house, I rule this crib
Change my diaper, son, where's my bib? ♪

10
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:42,417
♪ Don't pacify, you just got to pay me ♪

11
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,961
-♪ Who's in charge? ♪
-♪ Me, the Boss Baby ♪

12
00:00:48,965 --> 00:00:53,428
-[marker squeaking]
-[yawns]

13
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:58,391
[Boss Baby] What I've learned from
the airplane incident: Mega Fat CEO Baby,

14
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:02,062
that scooting diaper rash,
will stop at nothing to get me fired.

15
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:07,984
How do I protect my job? I need a very
big win. But from where? Concentrate.

16
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:11,571
-Hey! Here's just the pick-me-up we need.
-[jazz music playing]

17
00:01:11,654 --> 00:01:13,782
Hot poppin' jazz to keep me awake.

18
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:15,492
-[music gets louder]
-Nice. Ooh!

19
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:19,496
I love that jazz sizzlin'
in my little lady veins. Whoo-hoo! Yes!

20
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:22,957
It's eight o'clock. Can you turn to
the Goofball Chuck Nighttime Morning Show?

21
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:27,504
That's a no, daddy-o.
This jazz is like coffee for my ears.

22
00:01:27,587 --> 00:01:30,507
-Okay.
-[scatting]

23
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:34,552
-"Okay"?
-What? He's my dad. He said no.

24
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:40,016
[laughs] "No" is just the first word
in a very interesting conversation.

25
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:42,227
You have to think of parents
as adversaries

26
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,729
to be sliced to bits
at the negotiation table.

27
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:46,314
No, you think like that.

28
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:49,734
-I think of Mom and Dad as best friends.
-Oh, Templeton.

29
00:01:49,818 --> 00:01:50,902
[siren blaring]

30
00:01:51,444 --> 00:01:54,489
[gasps] Did we do crimes?
Are we gonna get arrested?

31
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:57,575
No, Tim.
I don't know why he's pulling us over.

32
00:01:57,659 --> 00:02:00,995
[blaring continues]

33
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:05,208
Turn off the jazz.
I don't want him to think we're ruffians.

34
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:11,422
What is it, officer?
Driving too carefully? [chuckles]

35
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:14,717
My new partner smelled trouble
and she's never wrong.

36
00:02:14,801 --> 00:02:16,719
Partner! Here, partner!

37
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:18,763
-Ahh!
-[meowing]

38
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:21,558
-[gasps]
-Ain't she cute as a nickel?

39
00:02:21,641 --> 00:02:24,644
But she's also tough as nails.
I call her Cat Cop.

40
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:26,271
-Cat Cop?
-Cat Cop.

41
00:02:26,354 --> 00:02:29,774
-Cat Cop?
-Cat Cop? [laughs]

42
00:02:29,858 --> 00:02:31,401
That is hilarious.

43
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:35,155
-[meowing]
-What's that, little partner?

44
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:37,991
-[meowing]
-Seems like there's a pretty big problem.

45
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:41,494
I'm gonna check it out.
Oh, broken taillight.

46
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:44,372
I'm pretty sure it wasn't broken
when we started driving.

47
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:50,962
-Hmm. Weird. I'll write you up a warning.
-[meowing]

48
00:02:51,045 --> 00:02:53,882
What's that, girl?
I should write a full-blown citation?

49
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:56,467
-[meows]
-Wait, I'm getting a ticket now

50
00:02:56,551 --> 00:02:59,053
-because of the cat?
-Do you have a problem

51
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,597
with my partner's judgment?

52
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:03,933
-[yowls]
-[gasps] No, officer, sir.

53
00:03:06,686 --> 00:03:10,815
Hey! Goo-goo ga-ga there!
Kind of funny, actually.

54
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:14,736
Cat Cop's been having me pull over
a heck of a lot of baby families lately.

55
00:03:14,819 --> 00:03:18,239
I had no idea folks with babies
were such troublemakers.

56
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:20,700
Anyway, have a nice night, folks.

57
00:03:20,783 --> 00:03:23,828
[growls]

58
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:27,248
What realm of dark flame
have we come home to?

59
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:30,418
[grunting]

60
00:03:31,794 --> 00:03:34,255
[sighs] Now, you're bringing in
the luggage for them?

61
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:38,051
-What? I love helping.
-Then come over here and help me.

62
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,761
-[Mom snoring]
-What's up?

63
00:03:39,844 --> 00:03:42,305
I'm trying to reconstruct what happened
while we were in Paris.

64
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:47,018
"Cat Cop given real badge.
Brought on as a police mascot,

65
00:03:47,101 --> 00:03:50,730
this former stray turned local hero
has quickly proven her worth.

66
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:53,566
After seeing the little kitten's
savvy nose for crime,

67
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:58,154
the chief has promoted Cat Cop from mascot
to an official member of the force."

68
00:03:58,238 --> 00:04:02,700
She's come a long way since her legendary
act of heroism in Dangerous Well Park.

69
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:08,039
"...said Cat Cop's partner, who's human
and not a cat." This is journalism?

70
00:04:08,122 --> 00:04:12,418
What's this legendary act of heroism
in Dangerous Well Park hoo-ha?

71
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:14,963
I don't buy it. Something's rotten.

72
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:20,635
Look! "Cat saves man from well.
The man had been in the well for hours.

73
00:04:20,718 --> 00:04:23,221
The gathering crowd had no clue
how to save him..."

74
00:04:23,304 --> 00:04:25,515
-Does anybody have a big stick?
-[meowing]

75
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:28,977
"...when a little stray kitten
came prancing up to the rescue."

76
00:04:31,437 --> 00:04:35,108
-[all cheering]
-[Boss Baby] No, this doesn't make sense.

77
00:04:35,191 --> 00:04:38,611
What kind of grown man gets stuck
in a well?

78
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:40,655
[both gasp]

79
00:04:40,738 --> 00:04:45,451
-It's Bootsy Calico!
-Of course! Oh, Bootsy, you went too far.

80
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:48,162
This is perfect! It solves everything.

81
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:50,832
-Uh... how?
-Stay with me, Templeton.

82
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:52,709
Calico's plots have always been ruthless,

83
00:04:52,792 --> 00:04:56,170
but up till now, there's been nothing
actually illegal, right?

84
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:57,463
Sure?

85
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,510
-"Oh, I'm Bootsy Calico."
-Nuh-uh.

86
00:05:02,593 --> 00:05:04,804
-That's Football Mike.
-Just go with it.

87
00:05:04,887 --> 00:05:08,182
"I opened a cat restaurant
to make people love cats.

88
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:12,228
I trained cats to sound like crying babies
so people hate babies.

89
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,771
No crimes here."

90
00:05:13,855 --> 00:05:15,982
Hold it right there, Bootsy!

91
00:05:16,065 --> 00:05:20,445
I shut your cat restaurant down,
I foiled your crybaby cat plot!

92
00:05:20,528 --> 00:05:24,032
"Oh, no, now, I'm desperate."
Here's Cat Cop.

93
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:25,825
-Um...
-I'm aware it's a dinosaur.

94
00:05:26,826 --> 00:05:30,580
Meow, meow. "I'm gonna stage a fake rescue
to get you on the police force

95
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:32,749
and make you do my evil bidding."

96
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:35,710
That is a crime! Fraud, corruption.

97
00:05:35,793 --> 00:05:39,213
You're going to jail. Bootsy goes down!
Boss Baby's a hero!

98
00:05:39,297 --> 00:05:42,216
Whoo! What do you think about that,
Mega Fat CEO Baby?

99
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:46,763
"Unter gunter! I'm going
to get you fired." Mega fat chance.

100
00:05:46,888 --> 00:05:52,226
Boom! [grunting] Try firing me now!
I'm the king of this company.

101
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:59,150
Ahh! I'm king of your face! [cackling]

102
00:05:59,233 --> 00:06:00,068
Templeton?

103
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:05,031
[grunting] You seemed busy,
so I went back to helping.

104
00:06:05,114 --> 00:06:09,535
No. No, no, no. I can't watch you
throw away your potential like this.

105
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:13,289
You're coming with me to Baby Corp.
I'm gonna bust Bootsy, protect my job,

106
00:06:13,372 --> 00:06:15,500
and give you your first lesson in...

107
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:18,086
power negotiating.

108
00:06:18,169 --> 00:06:19,712
[voice echoing]

109
00:06:21,172 --> 00:06:25,468
I need Mega Fat CEO Baby to approve
the gold star surveillance package.

110
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:27,637
State-of-the-art equipment,
sweet van, the works.

111
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,472
Isn't Mega Fat's office upstairs?

112
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:33,434
Rule one of negotiation:
never meet your adversary on their turf.

113
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:36,979
I thought negotiation was marching in
and being all, "Hey, I want this,

114
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:40,775
-so give it to me now, dummy!"
-No! Remain cool! Down to earth.

115
00:06:40,858 --> 00:06:44,403
And never ask for what you want.
Ask for more than what you want.

116
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:48,699
-Let them talk you down.
-Oh, so they think they won.

117
00:06:48,783 --> 00:06:50,952
I call them "smiling salami butts."

118
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:54,413
So happy,
no idea they've just been sliced to a nub.

119
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:58,376
There's our target, tossing back cookies

120
00:06:58,459 --> 00:07:01,170
-like he's his own grandma.
-I don't get it.

121
00:07:01,254 --> 00:07:06,342
Neither do I. Let's get that gold star
package. Mega Fat CEO Baby.

122
00:07:06,425 --> 00:07:07,969
The picture of good health.

123
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:12,890
Oh, Boss Baby, I'm so glad you survived

124
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:16,978
that airplane incident in which I had
no part you can prove, but I'm surprised

125
00:07:17,061 --> 00:07:20,189
you'd show your chubby cheeks
in here again so soon.

126
00:07:20,273 --> 00:07:22,900
He does have adorable chubby cheeks,
doesn't he?

127
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:25,111
Like a dainty chipmunk.

128
00:07:25,194 --> 00:07:27,697
So nice of you to say.

129
00:07:27,780 --> 00:07:31,200
Always a kind compliment
coming from your copious mouth.

130
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:34,162
Whatever you're buttering me up for,
the answer is no.

131
00:07:34,245 --> 00:07:37,457
I know how to take down
Bootsy Calico's entire operation.

132
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:41,002
Your request was pre-answered,
and the answer was "no."

133
00:07:41,085 --> 00:07:43,880
Wait, wait. Hold on, Magnus.
My ears are perky.

134
00:07:45,214 --> 00:07:50,928
All I need from you is... the platinum
supernova surveillance package.

135
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:53,222
Ha! Brown surveillance package for you.

136
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:56,726
Unacceptable!
Oh, I also need you to make me co-CEO.

137
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:59,604
That's too funny to laugh at.
I'm going to go ahead

138
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:03,900
-and keep trying to get you fired.
-So, how about we...

139
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:05,234
[cracks neck]

140
00:08:05,318 --> 00:08:06,319
...negotiate?

141
00:08:07,153 --> 00:08:08,821
[inaudible dialogue]

142
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:19,957
[inaudible dialogue]

143
00:08:23,669 --> 00:08:27,715
Gold star surveillance package. And if
you get Bootsy, I stop trying to fire you.

144
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:30,885
You get nothing else. Final.
I win. Shh! No more words.

145
00:08:30,968 --> 00:08:33,221
If that's all you can give me.

146
00:08:34,138 --> 00:08:38,142
[snickering] Sucker.
Do you think he heard that?

147
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:42,563
Mega Fat CEO Baby
has quietly called you a sucker.

148
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:44,232
You are the best, Magnus.

149
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:48,653
He's a smiling salami butt!

150
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:54,575
Meet your new best friend.
Baby's First Book of Negotiation.

151
00:08:54,825 --> 00:08:58,204
Learn it, live it.
I've got gold star surveilling to do.

152
00:08:58,996 --> 00:09:02,833
I deserve this.
I mean, it just feels right.

153
00:09:02,917 --> 00:09:07,421
[panting] Sorry I'm late.
Ooh, we're hugging cars?

154
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:08,839
-[chuckles]
-[car alarm blaring]

155
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:11,342
-[car beeps]
-All right, you two, listen up.

156
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:14,512
Step one,
catch Cat Cop in the act of dirty deeds.

157
00:09:14,595 --> 00:09:17,473
Step two, prove that Bootsy
is giving Cat Cop orders.

158
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:21,936
Step three, let the benevolent tsunami
of job security wash over me.

159
00:09:23,396 --> 00:09:25,523
-Where's Tim?
-He's a little busy...

160
00:09:26,023 --> 00:09:27,733
becoming incredible.

161
00:09:28,693 --> 00:09:32,947
No way this stuff works.
Mom, will you come here, please?

162
00:09:35,408 --> 00:09:36,909
What do you need, sweetie?

163
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:41,497
Um, well, first, you look great.
Picture of good health.

164
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:44,959
Weird compliment to get from my son,
but thank you.

165
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:48,754
You know what would really
be great for me? For all of us?

166
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:53,843
If I had a huge bowl of ice cream
for lunch. I'm thinking punch bowl?

167
00:09:53,926 --> 00:09:56,387
Ha! What? No.

168
00:09:56,470 --> 00:09:59,056
Okay, then. Um, maybe we should...

169
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:00,016
[neck cracks]

170
00:10:00,099 --> 00:10:01,517
...negotiate.

171
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:04,020
[inaudible dialogue]

172
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:13,237
[inaudible dialogue]

173
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,866
All right, one cone before lunch,
final offer.

174
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:20,661
Throw in a set of sprinkles,
and I think we have a deal.

175
00:10:21,912 --> 00:10:22,913
[gasps]

176
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:27,126
I'm eating ice cream
at 10:30 in the morning?

177
00:10:27,209 --> 00:10:28,794
This book is amazing.

178
00:10:30,171 --> 00:10:33,007
[baby cooing]

179
00:10:34,508 --> 00:10:38,679
-I got eyes on Cat Cop!
-[baby cooing]

180
00:10:39,722 --> 00:10:41,849
-[meows]
-[gasps]

181
00:10:48,564 --> 00:10:50,733
[meowing]

182
00:10:50,816 --> 00:10:53,027
What's that, partner?
Issue a jaywalking ticket?

183
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:57,656
-That dirty cat made her jaywalk!
-Jimbo, did you get that? Photo, video?

184
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:59,158
I can do that?

185
00:10:59,241 --> 00:11:02,328
Sorry. I'm used
to the brown surveillance package.

186
00:11:02,411 --> 00:11:05,581
♪ I'm a little kitty cat
Crossing the street ♪

187
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:07,333
[gasps] My evidence!

188
00:11:16,008 --> 00:11:16,926
[neck cracks]

189
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:20,221
[police siren, gunfire on TV]

190
00:11:20,304 --> 00:11:22,223
We're good parents.

191
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:28,771
[grunts]

192
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:33,943
Did you see that?
She broke the taillight! Jimbo?

193
00:11:34,026 --> 00:11:35,403
Got photos.

194
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:37,697
We got her!

195
00:11:38,864 --> 00:11:42,034
We could get Cat Cop off the police force
with this evidence.

196
00:11:42,118 --> 00:11:44,245
No! I don't just want Cat Cop.

197
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:47,498
My deal with Mega Fat was based
on busting Bootsy Calico.

198
00:11:47,581 --> 00:11:49,834
We have to connect Bootsy to this.

199
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:52,753
Team, this is one
of the most important moments--

200
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:56,257
-[Mom] Dinnertime! I'll get the baby!
-Bootsy connection. Find it.

201
00:11:57,508 --> 00:11:59,385
[cooing, sputtering]

202
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:02,805
-Negosh?
-Negosh.

203
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:03,931
Nice.

204
00:12:04,014 --> 00:12:07,935
So, I got pulled over twice today,
both times by Cat Cop.

205
00:12:08,018 --> 00:12:09,728
I feel like she's everywhere.

206
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:13,107
Three tickets for me since yesterday.
This is getting expensive.

207
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:14,233
-[doorbell rings]
-[meows]

208
00:12:14,316 --> 00:12:15,985
-Was that a meow?
-I'm unarmed!

209
00:12:16,068 --> 00:12:19,071
-[gasps] That can't be Cat Cop, can it?
-Not it!

210
00:12:20,406 --> 00:12:23,409
Kidding. I got you, Janice.
We'll go together.

211
00:12:24,326 --> 00:12:26,996
Man, this Cat Cop
 is really getting to Mom and Dad.

212
00:12:27,079 --> 00:12:30,374
Don't start feeling sorry for them,
Templeton. You'll lose your edge.

213
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:36,172
-Are you putting ice cream on your pizza?
-Anything I want. Negosh life to the max.

214
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:37,423
[monitor beeps]

215
00:12:37,506 --> 00:12:40,092
-We found Bootsy, BB.
-Go time. Where is he?

216
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:43,262
-He's walking into your house right now!
-What?

217
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,766
As I was saying,
once my restaurant closed,

218
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:50,102
I decided to get into real estate.

219
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:55,149
I just loved finding homes for food
in people's tummies so much,

220
00:12:55,232 --> 00:12:59,361
I figured, why not find actual homes
for real people?

221
00:12:59,445 --> 00:13:03,032
[chuckles] How quickly do y'all wanna
move out of this terrible town?

222
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:05,242
We've never actually considered moving.

223
00:13:05,326 --> 00:13:09,330
Oh, no? [scoffs] Seems like
every baby family is moving away,

224
00:13:09,413 --> 00:13:11,749
selling their houses to cat families.

225
00:13:11,832 --> 00:13:13,417
It's very trendy.

226
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:15,669
We do consider ourselves trendy.

227
00:13:15,753 --> 00:13:20,424
You most certainly are. Oh, geez Louise,
I may even buy this house myself.

228
00:13:20,508 --> 00:13:24,512
[chuckles] I bet this nice baby
would love to know my kitty cats

229
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:29,225
are frolicking around his old bedroom,
crib filled with kitty litter!

230
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:31,769
We'd probably take the crib with us.

231
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:35,731
Yes, I'd pay a lot of money
for a pretty little house like this.

232
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:41,862
-I'm sorry, did you say "a lot of money"?
-It's starting to making sense now.

233
00:13:41,946 --> 00:13:44,823
Bootsy's using Cat Cop
to harass baby families.

234
00:13:44,907 --> 00:13:47,701
Why? So he can drive babies out of town!

235
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:51,163
He's out there trying to get Mom and Dad
to sell him our house!

236
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:55,000
-What? Why would he even want our house?
-Don't you see, Templeton?

237
00:13:55,084 --> 00:13:58,087
 He's eliminating the competition.
Clear out all the baby families,

238
00:13:58,170 --> 00:14:00,923
 and this town becomes
nothing but a cat-ruled netherworld!

239
00:14:01,715 --> 00:14:05,302
-[ominous music playing]
-Can you open up?

240
00:14:05,386 --> 00:14:08,055
I just need something I left
at my old house.

241
00:14:12,351 --> 00:14:14,311
-[gasps]
-[cats yowling]

242
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:17,940
[thunder rumbling]

243
00:14:18,023 --> 00:14:19,650
[whimpers]

244
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:21,694
-[growling]
-[screams]

245
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:22,653
[snarls]

246
00:14:22,736 --> 00:14:25,155
-[screaming]
-[cats snarling]

247
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:27,241
[panting]

248
00:14:28,325 --> 00:14:30,286
-[gasps]
-[cats meowing]

249
00:14:30,369 --> 00:14:32,830
Football Mike, I'm so sorry I forgot you.

250
00:14:32,913 --> 00:14:38,002
Why did you let your parents sell
the house, Tim? Why? Hut, hut, help!

251
00:14:38,085 --> 00:14:40,170
No!

252
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:42,172
We can't move!

253
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:44,049
It's negosh time, baby.

254
00:14:45,426 --> 00:14:49,054
There's this sprucy new house
five towns from here.

255
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:51,390
And this one is even better.

256
00:14:51,473 --> 00:14:52,808
-It's farther.
-[door opens]

257
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:55,394
[neck cracks]

258
00:14:55,978 --> 00:15:01,275
You're making a huge mistake staying here!
Huge! And I don't know how you did it,

259
00:15:01,358 --> 00:15:05,029
but here's the $5 I agreed to give you.
Good day!

260
00:15:07,781 --> 00:15:12,161
Thanks for buying me some time.
Tonight, we bust Bootsy.

261
00:15:13,996 --> 00:15:16,206
You know, a little birdy told me

262
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:19,835
the Templetons
are causing all sorts of trouble.

263
00:15:20,377 --> 00:15:23,964
Someone from law enforcement
oughta straighten them out,

264
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:27,968
even if it takes lots and lots and lots
and lots of tickets.

265
00:15:28,052 --> 00:15:29,053
Don't you think?

266
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:38,604
-Jimbo?
-[Jimbo] We got him. Yay!

267
00:15:38,687 --> 00:15:41,982
Ugh, no, we didn't!
This just looks like a concerned citizen

268
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:45,903
-filing a grievance with a local officer.
-Come on, BB!

269
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:49,949
My job's on the line, Stace.
We pounce too soon, it all falls apart.

270
00:15:50,032 --> 00:15:54,411
This isn't enough.
We need solid, hard, concrete evidence.

271
00:15:54,495 --> 00:15:57,748
You two, I want 24/7 surveillance
on Bootsy Calico.

272
00:15:57,831 --> 00:15:59,333
What about Cat Cop?

273
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:03,212
We won't have to look for Cat Cop.
She'll be coming after my own family.

274
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:07,758
Oh! Since when is this a red curb?

275
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:21,313
-But that's not our litter.
-[siren blaring]

276
00:16:21,897 --> 00:16:26,193
Lucky for you, stealing a lawn gnome
is just a ticketable offense in this town.

277
00:16:26,276 --> 00:16:27,653
What lawn gnome?

278
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:31,699
-[meows]
-Oh, come on!

279
00:16:33,867 --> 00:16:37,162
I'm having a harder time convincing
Mom and Dad not to sell the house.

280
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:41,291
Cat Cop's really giving them,
pardon my language, big-time heck!

281
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:44,670
Negotiate strong, Templeton.
I'm fixing this as fast as I can.

282
00:16:44,753 --> 00:16:45,587
[monitor beeps]

283
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:49,425
Boss Baby, my man
with the gold star surveillance van.

284
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:51,802
That's super expensive equipment,
by the way.

285
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:55,264
I hope you got results because
I'd hate to tell the board of directors

286
00:16:55,347 --> 00:16:57,766
you're wasting money
 and they should let me fire you.

287
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:01,562
But, secretly, I'd love that so much,
I'd kiss it on the mouth. Mwah, mwah!

288
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:04,440
I love you, firing Boss Baby. Mwah, mwah!

289
00:17:04,523 --> 00:17:09,069
Save your kisses, Mega Fat.
I'm seconds away from nabbing Bootsy.

290
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:11,363
Please tell me we're seconds away
from nabbing Bootsy.

291
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:16,869
Ugh, no proof he's giving Cat Cop orders.
He hasn't left his lair in days.

292
00:17:16,952 --> 00:17:21,248
-I need action! I'm so bored!
-Not me.

293
00:17:21,331 --> 00:17:25,461
-I saw 102 cars go by.
-Not helpful, Jimbo.

294
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:27,629
Stace,
let me know the instant he makes a move.

295
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:29,381
-[Jimbo] 103--
-[clicks]

296
00:17:30,299 --> 00:17:32,718
-[grunts] Templeton!
-Sorry!

297
00:17:34,386 --> 00:17:38,307
[gasps] Wait. You gave me
the break I needed. Look at this.

298
00:17:38,390 --> 00:17:41,477
Bootsy's changing the battery
in Cat Cop's li'l helmet.

299
00:17:41,560 --> 00:17:43,729
-So?
-That's how he's giving orders.

300
00:17:43,812 --> 00:17:47,399
The helmet's a remote receiver,
and Bootsy's fingerprints are all over it.

301
00:17:47,983 --> 00:17:51,570
-So if we get Cat Cop's helmet...
-Bootsy's busted, baby!

302
00:17:51,653 --> 00:17:55,407
 I need a ride around the neighborhood
 to find Cat Cop and steal that helmet.

303
00:17:55,491 --> 00:17:57,951
You think I'm just gonna give
a bike ride away?

304
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:02,873
Oh, I could not be prouder of you,
monster I created. Let's do this!

305
00:18:02,956 --> 00:18:05,084
-[neck cracks]
-[neck cracks]

306
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:14,218
-[gasps] There's Cat Cop!
-[meowing]

307
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:19,890
[mutters] How was I supposed to know you
hated raisins? Oh, man. I sneezed on it.

308
00:18:19,973 --> 00:18:22,518
-Do we have a plan?
-We're gonna get that helmet.

309
00:18:22,726 --> 00:18:25,437
-[meows]
-I don't wanna get in trouble.

310
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:28,982
And I respect that. I'll come up
with a careful plan. There she is!

311
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:30,818
-[Boss Baby shouts]
-[yowls]

312
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:34,113
[cat snarling]

313
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:35,989
Hurry! Here comes her partner.

314
00:18:36,073 --> 00:18:39,993
I still can't get the helmet.
She's too wily. Give me a hand.

315
00:18:40,536 --> 00:18:44,206
-[both grunt]
-As they say in Dangerous Well Park,

316
00:18:44,289 --> 00:18:46,250
well, well, well.

317
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:48,961
The park has three wells.
 They're all dangerous.

318
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:52,089
Listen, officer,
maybe we can work something out.

319
00:18:52,172 --> 00:18:53,298
[neck cracks]

320
00:18:54,299 --> 00:18:58,846
Then he tried to negotiate his way
out of trouble, which really got my goat.

321
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:02,349
I'm gonna have to write you folks
a citation for loose children.

322
00:19:02,432 --> 00:19:04,059
-That's a big fine.
-[meows]

323
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:06,103
[sighs] Awesome. Thanks.

324
00:19:07,563 --> 00:19:09,857
These tickets are costing us a fortune.

325
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:12,609
 We have no choice
but to sell the house to Bootsy.

326
00:19:12,693 --> 00:19:15,904
Maybe a change will be good for Tim.
 He's really been acting out.

327
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:20,659
Yeah, all that negotiating. I'm starting
to feel like he's taking advantage of us.

328
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:26,999
[gasps] We're moving. Mom and Dad
turned into angry salami butts.

329
00:19:27,082 --> 00:19:29,501
-We didn't even get Cat Cop's helmet.
-[chuckles]

330
00:19:29,585 --> 00:19:33,255
-What are you so happy about?
-[laughs] We did get the helmet!

331
00:19:33,338 --> 00:19:36,967
-I swapped it out for Football Mike's!
-You can't take Football Mike's helmet.

332
00:19:37,050 --> 00:19:39,303
-That's what gives him football powers.
-Templeton,

333
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,597
 we've got Bootsy Calico dead to rights.

334
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:44,975
My job is safe. Mega Fat CEO Baby
won't be able to touch me

335
00:19:45,058 --> 00:19:49,271
-when I become the hero of Baby Corp.
-But we still have to move.

336
00:19:49,354 --> 00:19:54,151
Who cares? It's a simple real estate deal.
You get a new house. Play it right,

337
00:19:54,234 --> 00:19:58,322
and you can turn this into a full bedroom
suite upgrade, with hot tub!

338
00:19:58,405 --> 00:20:01,658
Come on, tiger. Get in there
and negosh like I taught you.

339
00:20:01,742 --> 00:20:05,829
You're just trying to teach me how
to be selfish! I don't wanna be like you!

340
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:10,709
I'm sorry about everything.
 I don't want us to move because of me.

341
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:14,713
[Mom] Oh, Timmy, it's not your fault.
Come here, baby.

342
00:20:15,255 --> 00:20:16,757
Am I a bad kid?

343
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:21,303
No! You're the best kid I know.
Come here. Big hug!

344
00:20:21,386 --> 00:20:26,808
[Mom] We love you, Tim, so much.
Nothing can ever change that.

345
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:30,187
[sighs]

346
00:20:39,905 --> 00:20:41,531
[cats snarling]

347
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:49,623
Bootsy Calico!

348
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:52,501
I'm here to negotiate.

349
00:20:52,584 --> 00:20:58,632
Ooh! Baby in a suit.
So, you've come into my lair to negotiate?

350
00:20:58,715 --> 00:21:03,720
I thought you were a smart businessman.
Oh, nice leverage.

351
00:21:04,721 --> 00:21:06,556
Your prints are all over this.

352
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:10,269
-This is a one-way ticket to prison.
-[gasps] The people pound?

353
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:12,312
I'm here to do business.

354
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,605
[neck cracks]

355
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:16,191
So, let's do business.

356
00:21:16,274 --> 00:21:17,484
[neck cracks]

357
00:21:18,860 --> 00:21:21,363
So, I'm pretty much
just gonna give this to you.

358
00:21:21,947 --> 00:21:26,576
All I ask is that Cat Cop is off the force
 and you pay all of my family's fines.

359
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:29,121
Wait a second. What's the play here?

360
00:21:29,204 --> 00:21:31,540
I just want my family to be happy again.

361
00:21:36,503 --> 00:21:40,924
Ooh-hoo-hoo!
Family's making you soft, baby man.

362
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:48,015
Mom and Dad's fines went away,
and the newspaper said Cat Cop quit.

363
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:51,143
You can go bust Bootsy Calico now.
We'll all be fine.

364
00:21:51,226 --> 00:21:54,229
I can't bust Bootsy anymore.
I gave him the helmet.

365
00:21:54,312 --> 00:21:56,690
What? Why? What about your job?

366
00:21:56,773 --> 00:21:59,735
You really think Mega Fat
has the brains to get me fired?

367
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:04,614
Just gonna be tougher to beat him now.
Besides, some things are more important,

368
00:22:04,698 --> 00:22:08,327
like proving to your brother
you're not as selfish as he thinks.

369
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:12,497
Oh, make no mistake.
I'm still selfish, but more self... ish?

370
00:22:14,291 --> 00:22:16,793
Is that Mr. Pineapple's Café?

371
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:21,340
I put a spy camera
in Cat Cop's helmet! [chuckles] Classic!

372
00:22:23,592 --> 00:22:26,887
-[Timmy] What's on the board?
-[gasps]

373
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:31,308
[Timmy] "Six well-placed kittens"?

374
00:22:31,391 --> 00:22:35,062
It looks like his master plan.
I think that's his master plan!

375
00:22:35,145 --> 00:22:39,524
Six well-placed kittens.
We got him. Let's get to work.

376
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:43,570
[theme song playing]

377
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:05,008
♪ Boss Baby ♪

